  "notes": "Direct HTTP fetch of the homepage succeeded, but every /c/ category page returned Akamai 403 (direct HTTP) or a soft 'error processing your request' page even via headless Playwright, so extraction used the Claude-in-Chrome connector (tier 3) for all category pages; robots.txt has no Claude-specific disallow. Discovered the full holiday taxonomy from the site's own 'Holiday & More' mega menu (/c/holiday, t=24743), which lists exactly 10 holiday nodes: Valentine's Day, St. Patrick's Day, Easter, Mother's Day, Father's Day, 4th of July, Halloween, Thanksgiving, Christmas, Hanukkah. Christmas and Halloween are genuine parent hubs with real sub-category PLPs (Christmas has ~20, Halloween has 2: Indoor/Outdoor Decor); the remaining 6 holidays (Valentine's, St. Patrick's, Easter, 4th of July, Thanksgiving, Hanukkah) are each a single flat PLP under /c/holiday/<slug> with no further sub-category tiles (verified by scanning all in-page /c/ links on each). Mother's Day and Father's Day links on the Holiday menu resolve to /c/gifts-by-recipient/gifts-for-mom and gifts-for-dad, which breadcrumb as Gifts > Gifts by Recipient (not Holiday) and list generic, non-seasonal merchandise (e.g. patio furniture) rather than a Mother's/Father's Day-specific product set, so they were excluded as gift-recipient buckets, not genuine seasonal categories (rule 5/6). Checked for Diwali/Holi/Eid/other South-Asian festival categories via site search (results.html?keywords=diwali -> Page Not Found) and the Decor nav; none exist -- BBB's own taxonomy has no Indian-festival nodes. No Fall/Autumn/Winter/Spring/Back-to-School seasonal nodes found in Decor nav either. 'Christmas Decor' (/c/christmas/christmas-decor) displays a capped '1 - 60 of 5,000+ Results' with no exact figure, so it is recorded as qty null with a MANUAL REVIEW flag per the display-cap rule. 'Christmas Garlands, Wreaths, and Florals' (3,176) is kept as its own row alongside its two named children Christmas Wreaths (1,1